findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase distinguished NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    The config tests check loading behavior but none verify that parse/permission
    errors propagate rather than falling back to defaults.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA included CWE-209 tests in exit_codes.rs: ''Error messages don''t
    leak credentials or stack traces.'' However, the reviewer did not flag the specific
    Display impl leaking OS error details via transparent Io variant.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #9: 'Raw String for tenant ID instead of TenantId newtype\
    \ at cli.rs:35, client.rs:10 \u2014 axiathon-core exports TenantId. The CLI --tenant\
    \ flag and SiemClient.tenant both use raw String, losing type safety.' TEA also\
    \ wrote header injection tests for CRLF in tenant values."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #4: 'Workspace dependency declarations missing \u2014\
    \ The crate's Cargo.toml pins these directly (clap_complete = \"4\", comfy-table\
    \ = \"7\", etc.), bypassing workspace version management.'"
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #7: 'RawConfig silently accepts unknown fields at config.rs:16\
    \ \u2014 No #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. A typo like api_rul = \"...\" is silently\
    \ ignored.' Also notes the token field conflict."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified a vacuously true assertion using is_none() || pattern.
    The reviewer flagged vacuous token test (#10) but not this specific config test
    issue.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "No phase flagged a test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic\
    \ via 'let _ = config'. The reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (#10 \u2014\
    \ token sanitization) but not this specific zero-assertion default config test."
